When starting work in this workspace, first run the workspace setup:

1. Pick an available workspace number (1-9) by checking: docker ps --format '{{.Names}}' | grep '^buurman-w'
2. Run: make workspace-setup WS=<number>
3. Add DNS entries if needed (check with: ping -c1 w<N>-app.local.buurman.io)
4. Start infrastructure: make dev
5. Wait ~30s for services to be healthy
6. Start backend: make backend
7. For frontend work: cd frontend && VITE_DEV_PORT=<port from setup output> VITE_HMR_PORT=<https_port> yarn dev:app

Port reference: WS=1→HTTPS:1443, WS=2→HTTPS:2443, etc.
See .conductor/setup.md for full details.